<title>USA: US Stockpile sells 13,189 lbs cadmium at 46.43c/lb.</title>
<headline>US Stockpile sells 13,189 lbs cadmium at 46.43c/lb.</headline>
<dateline>NEW YORK 1997-07-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>U.S. Defense Logistics Agency said Tuesday it sold 13,189 lbs of cadmium from the national stockpile to three firms at an average price of 46.43 cents a lb.</p>
<p>Atlas Metal Sales was the highest winning bidder at 55 cents a lb. Hall Chemical and Ney Smelting were the lowest winning bidders at 42 cents a lb. Hall Chemical was the largest bidder at 3,939 lbs.</p>
<p>DLA got $6,124.38 in the sale.</p>
<p>((New York Commodity Desk, 212-859-1646))</p>
</text>
